No product feature development may begin until the following foundation checks pass.

### Repository

- [ ] Git repository initialized.
- [ ] Conventional Commits configured.
- [ ] Native Git hooks configured.
- [ ] Branch protection configured.
- [ ] Required CI checks configured.

### Application

- [ ] Rust application compiles.
- [ ] SSR test page renders.
- [ ] Static assets are served.
- [ ] Health endpoints work.
- [ ] Graceful shutdown works.
- [ ] Configuration validation works.

### Development

- [ ] One-command startup works.
- [ ] Fresh checkout setup works.
- [ ] Database initializes automatically.
- [ ] Hot reload works where configured.
- [ ] Production preview works locally.

### Quality

- [ ] Formatter works.
- [ ] Linter works.
- [ ] Dependency auditing works.
- [ ] E2E tests run successfully.
- [ ] E2E tests run against a real application.
- [ ] JavaScript-disabled rendering is tested.
- [ ] Browser console errors are detected.

### Delivery

- [ ] GitHub Actions CI passes.
- [ ] Deployment workflow exists and is validated.
- [ ] Staging deployment works.
- [ ] Production deployment path is verified.
- [ ] Post-deployment health verification works.
- [ ] Rollback procedure is tested.

### Operations

- [ ] Structured logging works.
- [ ] Centralized error capture works.
- [ ] Performance telemetry works.
- [ ] Database migrations work.
- [ ] Backup and restore procedures are tested.
- [ ] Secret management is configured.
- [ ] Operational runbook exists.

Where live deployment requires credentials or infrastructure not yet supplied, prepare and validate everything possible, clearly mark the remaining external dependency, and never falsely report the deployment as verified.

