## 17. Final Rules

**Infrastructure must be boring.**

**Deployment must be automatic.**

**Tests must exercise real user journeys.**

**Development and production must share the same architecture.**

**The entire application must start with one command.**

**A monolith is the default, not a temporary compromise.**

**CI/CD must be simpler than the application it deploys.**

**Every deployment must be observable, verifiable, and recoverable.**

**Do not build infrastructure for hypothetical scale. Build the smallest system that can reliably serve actual users.**

The goal is a complete, maintainable, production-ready web engineering environment with the lowest reasonable operational complexity.

## Mandatory Standards-First Research — Context7 & Official Specifications

### Core rule

**Before implementing any browser-facing feature, ALWAYS research whether the web platform already provides a native solution.**

Never begin writing custom JavaScript, CSS workarounds, abstractions, polyfills, or third-party integrations before checking Context7 and the relevant official web standards.

The browser platform is the first dependency. Custom code is the last resort.

